# requirements-linux-py314.in: what requirements-linux-py314.lock holds
# beyond pyproject.toml's dependencies and its real-clients and
# voice-profile extras, which the lock compiles from pyproject.toml itself.
#
# The lock is the production install of a Linux server: CPython 3.14,
# x86_64, CPU-only torch from the PyTorch CPU index, every package at an
# exact version with its SHA-256s (docs/LINUX_HOST.md, "Install";
# scripts/linux/apply-update.sh, sync_deps). Regenerate it with
# scripts/linux/compile-linux-lock.sh, which runs pip-compile in a pinned
# python:3.14-slim container so the resolver sees Linux and Python 3.14
# whatever machine you run it on, and commit both files together.

# The speaker encoder behind voice profiles (domovoi/clients/voice_embedder.py).
# pyproject does not declare it (its webrtcvad pin has no Windows wheels);
# on Linux it installs normally, so the production lock carries it.
resemblyzer>=0.1.4

# The build backend: of this project (pip install --no-deps -e .) and of the
# few pins that publish only an sdist. The install builds them with
# --no-build-isolation against this hash-checked copy, so no build step
# downloads an unchecked setuptools of its own. Below 82: webrtcvad (under
# resemblyzer) imports pkg_resources, which setuptools 82 removed.
setuptools>=68,<82
